luded.** The APP instructions require an interactive, owner-visible PR for workflow changes; production APP source continues to move only through the owner’s promotion workflow. Do not mark ready, enable auto-merge or merge this infrastructure exception without that approval.\n\nActual artifact 13726823916 from deployment run [42736638074](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/42736638074) contained DEV `4efce3b0b` and `humans.js` SHA256 `9fb2d3cc7e5b968faaa010810b31c516a2c9a8f5a3a4530e7fedcd880a9db18e` with `clothHuman`. Inspected live requests instead returned DEV `c5382c727` and the baseline module SHA256 `5907dd17887953df9313d01c99d2a9c80aa5c8e4ef27ddea58c8199934456692`; encoded-path/cache-miss requests confirmed the mismatch. The Pages platform root cause remains **UNKNOWN**. This detector and a fresh legitimate MAIN revision do not guarantee an origin-selection fix; live results must establish delivery.\n\nThe three changed paths are:\n\n- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`\n- `.github/chicago-4d-preview-freshness.mjs`\n- `.github/test-chicago-4d-preview-freshness.mjs`\n\nThe new step runs after Pages deployment. Production continues to build MAIN; the preview continues to fetch current DEV, including on manual MAIN redeploys. Permissions, environment protection, concurrency, publication and deployment calls are unchanged. There are no `chicago/4d/` source or asset changes. A propagation delay beyond 120 seconds reports delivery as unverified rather than silently successful.\n\nValidation: six local HTTP-fixture tests passed in 0.620 seconds under the original 120-second supervisor cap, with no timeout override and complete owned-process cleanup. Cases cover matching files, HTTP 200 with an old revision, a current revision with an old carriage entrypoint, later propagation, HTTP errors and missing/overlong verification inputs. Parsed YAML comparison confirms the prior workflow structure and permissions are unchanged after removing the appended step. `